The invention concerns a process for forming and deburring gear teeth on workpieces (6). The process uses two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), and a deburring device (10). The workpieces (6) are automatically secured in the workpiece spindles (3, 3′), machined with the hobbing tool (12) to produce the teeth, and subsequently deburred. The process includes the following steps:

a. The first workpiece spindle (3) picks up an unmachined workpiece (6) at a first loading position (19) and conveys it to the hobbing tool (12);

b. A milling cut is performed;

c. The workpiece (6) is returned to the first loading position (19), after which another unmachined workpiece (6) is picked up;

d. The workpiece (6) on which the milling cut has been completed is transferred to a second loading position (19′);

e. At the second loading position (19′), the second workpiece spindle (3′) takes up the workpiece (6) and moves it to the deburring device (10);

f. The workpiece (6) is deburred.

An intermediate storage unit (14), capable of holding at least one workpiece (6), is arranged between the first and second loading positions (19, 19′). The workpiece (6) is transferred from this intermediate storage unit (14) to the second loading position (19′). Steps e and f are performed during the same time period in which step b is being carried out.

